+## Error paths in the session lifecycle
+
+Recorded by re-cinq/HALEngine#94, which moved the `beforeSession` call inside the orchestrator's `try`: a hook that throws at the top of the turn meets the same error path as any other failure in it, so a deployer who allocates in `beforeSession` and releases in `afterSession` does not leak the allocation on exactly the path where the allocation failed.
+
+- A `beforeSession` hook that throws rejects the turn to the caller with the error it threw, exactly as any other orchestrator failure rejects ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession for a throwing beforeSession and still rejects to the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- `onError` fires for a throw from `beforeSession`, handed the same session and the same `Error` the caller receives, and `afterSession` follows it — the order any other failed turn has ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession for a throwing beforeSession and still rejects to the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- `afterSession` cannot infer from its own invocation how much of the turn happened: when `beforeSession` threw, the session it receives carries exactly the entries it carried before the call, with no assistant entry opened and nothing left streaming, so a cleanup hook that must tell "never allocated" from "allocated and finished" reads the session, not the call ([validated by: hands afterSession a session the failed turn never touched](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L78)).
+
